            task: "Study construction estimating for my exam — review foundational concepts and methodology: types of estimates and project phases (order of magnitude estimate: ±30–50%, used in feasibility — cost per square foot or unit comparison with historical data; schematic design estimate: ±15–20%, assemblies-based using systems cost; design development estimate: ±10–15%, more detailed systems takeoff; construction document estimate: ±5–10%, detailed quantity takeoff and unit prices; bid estimate: contractor's final pricing with complete drawings and specifications); quantity takeoff fundamentals (reading plans: architectural, structural, mechanical, electrical, plumbing drawings; scales and dimensions; area calculations: floor area, wall area, roof area — gross vs net; linear measurements: perimeter, linear feet of pipe, conduit, framing; volume calculations: concrete cubic yards, earthwork cubic yards; counting units: doors, windows, fixtures, light fixtures; waste and coverage factors by material type); CSI MasterFormat divisions (Division 01 General Requirements; Division 03 Concrete: formwork, rebar, ready-mix; Division 04 Masonry: CMU, brick, mortar; Division 05 Metals: structural steel, miscellaneous metals; Division 06 Wood/Plastics: rough framing, finish carpentry, millwork; Division 07 Thermal/Moisture: insulation, roofing, waterproofing; Division 08 Openings: doors, windows, hardware; Division 09 Finishes: drywall, paint, flooring, tile; Division 10+ Specialties through Division 48 Electrical Power Generation); pricing methods (RSMeans: unit price database — labor, material, equipment costs by CSI division; crew makeup and crew productivity; bare cost vs total cost including overhead and profit; location factor adjustment by city index; assemblies cost data — system cost per SF for common building systems; unit price estimating: quantity × unit price = extension; summarizing the estimate: direct job costs + general conditions + overhead + profit + contingency = contract price); bid strategy and subcontractor management (invitation to bid, scope of work, addenda, substitutions; bid form completion: lump sum, unit price, allowances, alternates; reviewing sub bids: comparison matrix, leveling subs, scope gaps; bonding: bid bond, performance bond, payment bond requirements; general conditions cost: superintendent, project manager, temporary facilities, insurance, permits)",
