ymptom onset; neuroinflammation: microglial activation → TNF-α, IL-1β, IL-6 → oxidative stress → mitochondrial dysfunction; senescent neurons: p21, p16 markers, SASP — secretory phenotype that propagates inflammation; blood-brain barrier aging: pericyte loss, tight junction degradation, increased permeability); biomarkers and imaging (CSF biomarkers: Aβ42 ↓, p-tau ↑, total tau ↑ in AD; PET imaging: amyloid PET (florbetapir, PiB), tau PET (flortaucipir), FDG-PET for metabolic decline; structural MRI: hippocampal atrophy, cortical thinning in AD; DaTscan: striatal dopamine transporter loss in PD; blood biomarkers: plasma Aβ42/40 ratio, p-tau217, NfL for neurodegeneration)",
