n troglodytes, Pan paniscus (bonobos — female-dominated, sexual conflict resolution), Gorilla (sexual dimorphism, silverback), Pongo (arboreal, orangutans); ape cognition: theory of mind, mirror self-recognition, tool use — chimpanzee nut cracking, fishing for termites; de Waal on reciprocal altruism and social politics); osteology and bioarchaeology (bone identification: cortical vs trabecular bone; skeletal indicators of age: epiphyseal fusion, dental eruption, pubic symphysis morphology (Todd method, Brooks and Suchey), auricular surface, cranial suture closure; sex estimation: pelvic morphology — greater sciatic notch, subpubic angle, obturator foramen; cranial — supraorbital ridge, mastoid process, mental eminence; skeletal indicators of disease: porotic hyperostosis (iron-deficiency anemia), cribra orbitalia, Harris lines (growth disruption), periosteal reaction, dental caries, DISH; stature estimation: regression formulas from long bones (Trotter and Gleser))",
