ng pelvic morphology (three traits), estimate stature using one long bone regression formula; describe paleopathological observations — periosteal reaction, porotic hyperostosis, dental caries, Harris lines, DISH; interpret the health implications for the population; discuss taphonomy — how did post-depositional processes affect preservation and interpretability?; conclude with what the skeletal data reveal about health, diet, or activity patterns in this population)",
