point pre-specification)); biomarker development (FDA-NIH Biomarker Working Group BEST glossary: susceptibility/risk, diagnostic, monitoring, predictive (treatment response), prognostic, pharmacodynamic/response, safety biomarkers; biomarker qualification: analytical validation (precision, accuracy, reproducibility, LLOQ) → clinical validation (association with outcome) → clinical utility (improves decisions); surrogate endpoints: FDA accelerated approval — surrogate reasonably likely to predict clinical benefit; surrogate endpoint examples: LDL-C for CV events, blood pressure for stroke, HbA1c for diabetic complications; companion diagnostics: FDA co-development framework for targeted therapies — PD-L1 for pembrolizumab, EGFR mutation for erlotinib); regulatory science (FDA Center for Drug Evaluation and Research (CDER) and Center for Biologics Evaluation and Research (CBER); PDUFA dates; priority review, breakthrough therapy designation, fast track, accelerated approval; EMA parallel scientific advice; adaptive trial designs: response-adaptive randomization, seamless phase 2/3, platform trials, basket trials, umbrella trials)",
