es to long-term goals; types of evaluation: process/implementation, outcome, impact; impact evaluation: random assignment (RCT), difference-in-differences, regression discontinuity, instrumental variables; counterfactual: what would have happened without the program? Internal validity vs external validity tradeoff; stakeholder analysis: identify all actors, their interests, level of influence, and position (support/oppose/neutral); power-interest grid); federalism and implementation (principal-agent problem in policy implementation: bureaucratic discretion, street-level bureaucrats (Lipsky); cooperative vs coercive federalism; block grants vs categorical grants; regulatory federalism: preemption, mandates; implementation failure types: program theory failure vs implementation failure)",
            successCriteria: "Public policy study session completed (Bardach's eightfold path steps named in order, Kingdon's three streams and policy window concept explained, cost-benefit analysis discount formula stated, logic model components named, and exam notes saved)",
