l/child mortality, strengthen health systems; interlinkages: SDG 1 (poverty), SDG 2 (hunger), SDG 6 (water), SDG 13 (climate)); health systems and universal health coverage (UHC) (WHO six building blocks: service delivery, health workforce, health information systems, access to essential medicines, financing, governance/leadership; UHC cube: population covered, services covered, cost covered; Alma-Ata Declaration (1978): primary health care, Health for All; Astana Declaration (2018): renewed PHC commitment; health financing: Beveridge (tax-funded), Bismarck (social insurance), out-of-pocket (catastrophic expenditure); out-of-pocket spending and financial risk protection: catastrophic health expenditure threshold (40% of household income after subsistence); essential medicines: WHO Essential Medicines List (EML), TRIPS flexibilities, generic production, Doha Declaration; health workforce crisis: WHO projection — 18M shortage by 2030 in LMICs; tropical medicine: malaria lifecycle (Plasmodium falciparum, P. vivax — anopheles vector, hepatic and erythrocytic stages; chloroquine resistance; artemisinin-combination therapy (ACT)); tuberculosis (Mycobacterium tuberculosis; directly observed therapy short-course (DOTS); drug-resistant TB: MDR-TB, XDR-TB; BCG vaccine; HIV-TB co-infection); HIV/AIDS (global epidemiology: 39M living with HIV; UNAIDS 95-95-95 targets; antiretroviral therapy (ART) mechanisms); cholera (Vibrio cholerae, oral rehydration therapy, oral cholera vaccine; Haiti 2010 outbreak))",
