ng mix: government spending (% of GDP), donor contributions, and out-of-pocket expenditure (% of total health spending); compute or interpret the catastrophic health expenditure rate (households spending >40% of income on health after subsistence); identify the primary financing gap — shortfall from the WHO benchmark of $86 USD per capita for essential services; describe one reform option: social health insurance expansion, community-based health insurance, results-based financing, or user fee elimination with compensatory financing; use the UHC service coverage index (SCI) as the outcome measure — what score does the country have and what sub-indicators drive it?; conclude with the most feasible reform given the country's political economy and institutional capacity)",
