 peaks day 3–5; pathologic jaundice within 24 h → hemolytic disease; phototherapy thresholds by gestational age (Bhutani nomogram); exchange transfusion for severe hyperbilirubinemia; neonatal hypoglycemia: glucose < 47 mg/dL symptomatic; IV dextrose 10% at 2 mL/kg bolus; glucose infusion rate (GIR) calculation; necrotizing enterocolitis (NEC): premature infants, bloody stools, abdominal distension; pneumatosis intestinalis on X-ray; NPO, antibiotics, surgery for perforation; retinopathy of prematurity (ROP): excessive O2 → neovascularization; screen at 31 weeks PMA or 4 weeks postnatal; laser photocoagulation or bevacizumab)",
