 in NICU; catheter-related; empiric vancomycin + gram-negative coverage; lumbar puncture if septic (CSF culture); TORCH infections: Toxoplasmosis, Other (syphilis, VZV, parvovirus), Rubella, CMV, HSV — congenital anomalies, microcephaly, hepatosplenomegaly, petechiae, SNHL; intraventricular hemorrhage (IVH): germinal matrix hemorrhage; Papile grading I–IV; head ultrasound at 7–10 days for < 32 weeks; prevention: antenatal steroids, indomethacin, normoglycemia, gentle ventilation; hydrocephalus, periventricular leukomalacia (PVL) complications)",
