s present in food (heme vs non-heme iron; calcium carbonate vs calcium citrate; zinc from meat vs legumes; D2 vs D3); identify three dietary factors that enhance and three that inhibit absorption; calculate the estimated absorbed quantity from a sample 1-day diet using bioavailability conversion factors; compare bioavailability from food vs supplement; identify the population most at risk for deficiency of this nutrient and one screening test used)",
