 gonorrhea; benzathine penicillin G 2.4 million units IM for primary/secondary syphilis; discuss partner notification: confidential partner notification, expedited partner therapy (EPT); describe one long-term complication of untreated disease: PID → infertility/ectopic pregnancy risk for untreated chlamydia; discuss one harm reduction approach for STI prevention in this population), or a reproductive justice analysis (define reproductive justice (SisterSong): three rights — right to have children, right to not have children, right to parent children in safe communities; compare reproductive rights (individual liberty) to reproductive justice (structural/social justice lens); identify one historical reproductive rights violation in the U.S.: forced sterilization of Native American women (Indian Health Service), Puerto Rican sterilization campaign, or Buck v. Bell (1927) forced sterilization law; apply an intersectionality analysis: how do race, class, immigration status, disability, and geography affect reproductive autonomy?; describe one current policy that restricts reproductive health access (e.g., state abortion restrictions, Medicaid funding restrictions, contraceptive coverage mandates); evaluate one community-based intervention that advances reproductive justice: doula programs for Black mothers, school-based health centers, Title X family planning funding)",
