egration and assimilation policy: linguistic integration — English language acquisition; civic integration — naturalization policy; structural integration — housing, education, labor market access; segmented assimilation theory (Portes/Zhou): different integration paths for different immigrant groups; USCIS naturalization policy; state vs federal immigration authority: Arizona v United States (2012): federal preemption of state immigration enforcement; E-Verify; 287(g) partnerships; immigration and social policy: PRWORA (1996) — welfare reform barred most immigrants from federal benefits for 5 years after admission; public charge rule)",
