lth information (PHI) — 18 identifiers; covered entities + business associates; minimum necessary principle; patient rights: access, amendment, accounting of disclosures; Notice of Privacy Practices; HIPAA enforcement: HHS OCR; Breach Notification Rule: 60-day notification to individuals + HHS for breaches ≥500 records; state data breach notification laws: all 50 states have breach notification laws — variation in definition of breach, timing, scope; cross-border data transfers (Schrems I (2015): CJEU invalidated EU-US Safe Harbor — U.S. surveillance law incompatible with GDPR adequacy; Schrems II (2020): CJEU invalidated Privacy Shield; Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs) may be used but must be assessed against U.S. law; adequacy decisions: UK, Switzerland, Israel, Japan, South Korea; EU-US Data Privacy Framework (DPF, 2023): new adequacy mechanism; Schrems III threat; data localization: Russia (FZ-242), China PIPL (cross-border transfer conditions), India DPDP Act (2023))",
