l to deal — Aspen Skiing; United States v Microsoft (D.C. Cir. 2001): browser bundling as exclusionary conduct; attempted monopolization: dangerous probability of success + specific intent; US v Google LLC (DDC 2024): exclusive default search agreements as exclusionary conduct); Clayton Act and merger review (Section 7: prohibits acquisitions that may substantially lessen competition or tend to create a monopoly; DOJ/FTC Merger Guidelines (2023): new framework — market concentration, competitive effects, entry analysis; HHI thresholds: post-merger HHI >2500 and increase >200 — presumptively anticompetitive; Hart-Scott-Rodino (HSR) Act: pre-merger notification; DOJ and FTC second request; remedies: structural (divestiture) vs behavioral consent decrees; EU competition law (EU Article 101 TFEU: agreements between undertakings that restrict competition — four elements + block exemptions (vertical BER, horizontal BER); Article 101(3) exemption; Article 102 TFEU: abuse of dominant position — dominance threshold (typically >40–50% market share); exclusionary abuse (predatory pricing, exclusive dealing, refusal to supply, margin squeeze); exploitative abuse (excessive pricing); EU merger regulation (EC Regulation 139/2004): SIEC test (significant impediment to effective competition))",
