omic cycles by forcing banks to deleverage in recessions? How does the countercyclical capital buffer address this?; evaluate the tension between safety and credit supply: does the capital requirement reduce bank lending to the real economy?; analyze U.S. implementation: how did Dodd-Frank and the Fed's enhanced prudential standards implement Basel III? How did the Basel III endgame (2023 proposal) expand the framework?; evaluate the leverage ratio as a complement to risk-weighted capital: does a simple leverage constraint better prevent manipulation of risk weights?; apply to one contemporary concern: does Basel III adequately address climate risk, crypto-asset exposure, or the failures of Silicon Valley Bank (2023)?), or a community banking / CRA analysis (select one community banking law issue: CRA compliance and LMI lending obligations, FDIC resolution of a community bank failure, OCC fair access rule, CFPB supervision of community banks, or the 2023 CRA modernization rule; describe the relevant statute or rule and its key requirements; apply the dual banking system: does the community bank in question operate under a national charter (OCC) or state charter (Fed/FDIC)? What regulatory differences follow?; analyze CRA obligations: what credit, investment, and service activities qualify for CRA credit? How are CRA ratings determined, and what are the consequences of a Needs to Improve or Substantial Noncompliance rating?; apply redlining history: how does the CRA respond to the history of discriminatory mortgage lending? What structural limits does the CRA have?; evaluate the 2023 CRA modernization rule: how did the OCC, Fed, and FDIC update the CRA framework for digital banking and fintech partnerships?; discuss one contemporary challenge: how does fintech competition, credit union exemptions, or BNPL (buy now pay later) lending affect the regulatory gap the CRA was designed to fill?; propose one reform to better serve the CRA's equity and access goals in the digital banking era)",
