ds Act (ESSA, 2015): replaced NCLB; returned accountability authority to states; required evidence-based interventions in bottom 5% of schools; multi-metric accountability: not just test scores); teacher effectiveness (teacher quality: value-added models (VAMs): estimate teacher contribution to student learning above baseline; Chetty, Friedman, Rockoff (2014): having a higher VA teacher in 4th grade increases lifetime earnings; concerns about VAM stability, construct validity, gaming; MET Project (Gates Foundation): VAMs, classroom observations, and student surveys as multi-measure evaluation; teacher tenure and dismissal: Vergara v California (2014) — tenure statutes found unconstitutional for concentrating ineffective teachers in low-income schools; Teach for America: short-term placement of high-ability graduates; evidence on TFA effectiveness: Glazerman et al., Xu et al.); higher education policy (college wage premium: Goldin and Katz — race between education and technology; free college proposals: Sanders/Biden free community college; Kelchen et al. on net tuition vs list price; student debt: $1.7T U.S. student loan debt; income-driven repayment (IDR) plans; Biden loan forgiveness; Bennett hypothesis: does federal aid increase tuition?; college rankings and signaling; accountability: gainful employment rule; HEA reauthorization; for-profit college sector collapse: Corinthian, ITT)",
