 — how do VAMs, classroom observations (Framework for Teaching), and student perception surveys (Tripod) correlate? Which measure best predicts student achievement gains? Evaluate the construct validity of each; evaluate tenure and dismissal policy — apply Vergara v California: what does the court find about ineffective teacher distribution? What are the tradeoffs between tenure (teacher security, investment in school) and dismissal flexibility (removing ineffective teachers)?; evaluate TFA impact — apply Glazerman et al. (2004) random assignment study vs Xu et al.: what do lottery and observational estimates of TFA teacher effectiveness show? How does TFA effectiveness compare to traditionally certified teachers?), or a higher education policy analysis (select one: evaluate income-driven repayment (IDR) and loan forgiveness policy — apply the Bennett hypothesis: does federal student aid increase tuition at the margin? What does the evidence from Pell Grant increases and institutional aid suggest?; evaluate the evidence on the college wage premium — apply Goldin-Katz's 'race between education and technology': how has the premium evolved since 1980? What does the premium measure when signaling contributes to returns?; evaluate free college proposals — what is the distributional effect of free community college vs free four-year college? Who currently doesn't attend college due to cost vs other barriers?; evaluate the for-profit college sector and accountability — apply the gainful employment rule: what does the evidence on for-profit outcomes (Deming, Goldin, Katz, 2012) show? What regulatory mechanisms (80/20 rule, cohort default rates, gainful employment) have been effective at improving outcomes or reducing harm?; evaluate college rankings and their effects on institutional behavior)",
