gulatory oversight?; evaluate Islamic law in Muslim-minority contexts — apply the argument that Islamic law in Europe and North America functions through private ordering (Islamic marriage contracts, arbitration, charitable waqf endowments) rather than state enforcement; evaluate the UK Shari'a Council and Muslim Arbitration Tribunal: what legal status do their decisions have? What equality law tensions arise from gender-differentiated fiqh rules in a liberal democratic context?; evaluate classical waqf (endowment) law and its contemporary revival — what is the perpetuity requirement in waqf? How does cash waqf work? Evaluate waqf as a vehicle for Islamic social finance (hospitals, schools, poverty relief) in contemporary Muslim-majority states and diaspora communities)",
