od order quantity (POQ); pegging; capacity requirements planning (CRP)); ERP systems (ERP architecture: integrated database vs best-of-breed; SAP modules: MM (materials management), PP (production planning), SD (sales and distribution), FI (finance), CO (controlling); Oracle Supply Chain; ERP implementation challenges: change management, data migration, customization vs configuration); revenue management (yield management: price discrimination across customer segments; EMSR (expected marginal seat revenue) model: protect seats for high-fare class if E[high-fare] ≥ low-fare; overbooking: net benefit = P(show) × revenue - P(no-show) × denied boarding cost; dynamic pricing; hotel/airline/car rental applications; capacity planning (bottleneck capacity: bottleneck = resource with lowest capacity rate; utilization = demand/capacity; capacity planning: timing (lead/lag/match strategies), sizing (economies of scale), type (general vs dedicated))",
