wey worker earnings, Hoynes-Schanzenbach SNAP, or within-firm productivity studies); evaluate the two-way fixed effects estimator and its recent critics — apply Goodman-Bacon (2021) decomposition and Callaway-Sant'Anna (2021): what does TWFE estimate under treatment effect heterogeneity? How does the negative weighting problem arise? Evaluate proposed solutions; apply to a specific staggered policy adoption; evaluate cluster standard errors and inference — apply the Liang-Zeger (1986) sandwich estimator: when should errors be clustered and at what level? Evaluate the Cameron-Gelbach-Miller wild cluster bootstrap for small numbers of clusters; what is the consequence of incorrect standard error clustering for inference on minimum wage or policy studies?; evaluate a synthetic control analysis — apply Abadie-Diamond-Hainmueller (2010) synthetic control to a specific case (Card 2010 German reunification, Dube-Zipperer 2015 minimum wage, or Abadie-Gardeazabal 2003 Basque terrorism): how does synthetic control differ from DiD? What determines the pre-period fit? Evaluate the permutation-based inference approach; or a cross-sectional causal inference analysis (select one: evaluate the Bartik (shift-share) instrument — apply Goldsmith-Pinkham-Sorkin-Swift (2019): what conditions make the Bartik instrument valid? Is validity driven by the shares or the shifts? Evaluate the Borusyak-Hull-Jaravel (2022) alternative: what does a rotational invariance argument imply for valid instruments?; evaluate matching and propensity score methods — apply Dehejia-Wahba (1999) and LaLonde (1986) benchmark: what is the propensity score (Rosenbaum-Rubin 1983); evaluate overlap and common support; compare nearest-neighbor, kernel, and IPW matching; what are the key assumptions (unconfoundedness, SUTVA)? Evaluate doubly-robust estimators; evaluate regression kink design (Nielsen-Sørensen-Taber 2010) — how does a kink in the assignment rule identify treatment effects? What conditions are required? Apply to a specific kinked policy (UI benefits, marginal tax rates, health insurance subsidies))",
