urity: who controls the food system matters, not just whether food is available; right to food in international law: Article 25 UDHR; ICESCR Article 11; UN Special Rapporteur on Right to Food; agroecology as alternative paradigm: Gliessman, IPES-Food; debates: agroecology vs Green Revolution productivity; local vs global food systems; Codex Alimentarius: FAO/WHO joint body for international food standards; sets standards for food safety, labeling, additives, pesticide MRLs; adopted as WTO SPS baseline; food price crises and governance (2007–2008 food price crisis: wheat, rice, maize prices tripled; causes — ethanol mandate (U.S. Renewable Fuel Standard), export bans (Russia, Ukraine), commodity speculation, dollar depreciation, supply shocks; effects: food riots in 40+ countries; 2010–2012 food price spike; role of food price volatility in Arab Spring; G20 Agricultural Market Information System (AMIS); World Food Programme (WFP) operations: emergency food aid, school feeding, cash transfers; FAO technical assistance and norm-setting)",
