 points for transitioning away from industrial monocultures?; evaluate the WTO Agreement on Agriculture (AoA) and its effects on developing country food systems — how do Green Box subsidies (permitted domestic support), Amber Box (production-linked support), and export subsidies affect international agricultural markets? What is the Special Safeguard Mechanism debate for developing countries?; evaluate land grabbing — apply the Tirana Declaration and the Voluntary Guidelines on Responsible Governance of Tenure (VGGT): what drives large-scale land acquisitions in Africa and Southeast Asia? What effects on local food security, smallholder farmers, and food sovereignty has evidence documented?), or a Green Revolution and agricultural development analysis (select one: evaluate the Green Revolution's distributional effects — what were the gains in wheat and rice productivity in South Asia? Which farmers benefited and which were left behind? What is the evidence on the Green Revolution's effect on rural wages and poverty? Evaluate the Green Revolution's environmental costs: aquifer depletion, pesticide use, genetic erosion, soil salinity; evaluate the Africa Green Revolution debate — apply AGRA's programs vs the agroecological alternative (IPES-Food): what does the evidence say about hybrid seed adoption, fertilizer subsidies, and yield gains in sub-Saharan Africa? What structural barriers (market access, infrastructure, credit) limit technology adoption?; evaluate the role of commodity traders in global food supply chains — apply Clapp's analysis of financialization: how do ABCD firms (Cargill, ADM, Bunge, Louis Dreyfus) shape global commodity flows, price discovery, and food system governance? What evidence links commodity derivatives markets to food price volatility?; evaluate organic and agroecological transition pathways — apply the Cuba Special Period case study or the Danish organic action plan: what conditions enable a large-scale agroecological transition? What are the food security implications?)",
