of small-worldness: σ=C/C_r ÷ L/L_r > 1); community detection (community structure: groups with dense internal, sparse external connections; modularity Q=Σ_c[L_c/m - (d_c/(2m))²] where L_c intra-community edges, m total edges, d_c community volume; maximum Q partitioning is NP-hard; Louvain algorithm: greedy modularity maximization in two phases (local moves, community aggregation), scales to billion-node networks; spectral methods: Fiedler vector (second eigenvector of Laplacian L=D-A); stochastic block model (SBM): generative model for communities; label propagation; resolution limit of modularity: cannot detect communities smaller than O(√m); overlapping communities: BIGCLAM, node2vec); percolation theory (bond percolation: each edge retained with probability p; site percolation: each node retained with probability p; for ER: giant component emerges at p_c=1/⟨k⟩; order parameter: size of giant component S(p); S(p)~(p-p_c)^β near threshold (β=1 for ER); for scale-free (2<γ<3): p_c→0 (no threshold) because ⟨k²⟩/⟨k⟩→∞; network resilience: random failure vs targeted attack (removal of highest-degree hubs drastically reduces p_c); k-core decomposition: iteratively remove nodes with degree<k; innermost core = most resilient backbone; cascading failures: overload redistribution models (Motter-Lai)); epidemic spreading (SIR model: Susceptible-Infected-Recovered; β infection rate, μ recovery rate; on networks: effective spreading rate λ=β/μ; epidemic threshold λ_c=⟨k⟩/⟨k²⟩; for ER: λ_c=1/⟨k⟩; for scale-free (γ≤3): λ_c→0 as N→∞ (vanishing threshold — any transmission causes epidemic); SIS model: no immunity, endemic state; R₀=β⟨k⟩/μ for homogeneous mixing; heterogeneous mean-field: consider degree classes separately; network interventions: targeted vaccination of hubs (acquaintance immunization: vaccinate a random neighbor of a random node — exploits friendship paradox); contact tracing on networks; temporal networks: epidemic dynamics on time-varying networks)",
            successCriteria: "Network science study session completed (ER giant component threshold stated, BA preferential attachment power-law exponent given, Watts-Strogatz high-C/low-L property explained, modularity Q formula written, scale-free epidemic threshold derived as zero, and exam notes saved)",
