ction network); evaluate spectral community detection — derive the spectral partitioning from the graph Laplacian L=D-A: why is the Fiedler vector (second-smallest eigenvector) the optimal partition for graph bisection? What is the Cheeger inequality connecting algebraic connectivity to the conductance of the cut? Evaluate the normalized vs unnormalized Laplacian; apply to network flow problems; evaluate dynamic community detection in temporal networks — apply the multilayer graph formulation (Mucha et al. 2010): how does the coupling parameter ω between time layers control the temporal resolution of community detection? What is the appropriate ω for detecting communities in a social network vs a financial correlation network?; evaluate node embedding methods (node2vec, DeepWalk) as alternatives to spectral methods for community detection and link prediction), or a spreading and robustness analysis (select one: evaluate epidemic spreading on heterogeneous networks — apply the heterogeneous mean-field (HMF) theory: write degree-stratified rate equations for the SIS model; derive the epidemic threshold λ_c = ⟨k⟩/⟨k²⟩; show that for power-law networks with γ≤3, λ_c→0 as N→∞; evaluate the quenched mean-field (QMF) and N-intertwined mean-field approximation (NIMFA) as refinements; apply to evaluate the effectiveness of targeted vs random immunization and acquaintance immunization; evaluate network percolation and cascading failures — derive the giant component size for ER networks using the generating function formalism (Molloy-Reed condition: ⟨k(k-2)⟩=0 at threshold); extend to configuration model; apply to evaluate the vulnerability of scale-free vs ER networks to targeted hub removal and to random failure; model a cascading failure using the load redistribution (Motter-Lai) model and evaluate the relationship between initial load distribution and cascade size; evaluate link prediction methods — apply the common neighbors, Jaccard coefficient, Adamic-Adar index, and preferential attachment score as link prediction heuristics; evaluate the node2vec embedding approach: what does the hyperparameter trade-off between BFS and DFS walks control? Apply the area under the ROC curve as evaluation metric on a held-out test set of edges; discuss the distinction between structural equivalence and regular equivalence in predicting link formation)",
