ghting adopted by Netherlands)? Evaluate Dolan-Tsuchiya evidence on public preferences for health priority setting: do respondents accept QALY maximization or do they prefer equity weights? Apply to a specific technology appraisal (CAR-T cell therapy, GLP-1 agonists, or a gene therapy): derive the ICER, apply the NICE end-of-life modifier, and evaluate whether the therapy should be approved at the standard threshold; evaluate the ICER (Institute for Clinical and Economic Review) framework for drug pricing — apply to a specific drug (semaglutide for obesity, lecanemab for Alzheimer's, or a rare disease gene therapy): what value-based price does ICER calculate, and how does the actual launch price compare? Evaluate the role of budget impact analysis alongside cost-effectiveness; what is the socially acceptable ICER threshold for the US and what does it imply for insurance coverage mandates?; evaluate health technology assessment and differential access — apply the Bismarck vs Beveridge framework to pharmaceutical coverage decisions: why do Beveridge-model countries with global budgets more readily implement QALY-based rationing than social insurance countries with benefit mandates? Evaluate the FDA vs EMA regulatory frameworks and their interaction with HTA; what is the role of patient advocacy in HTA decisions for rare diseases?), or a social determinants and health equity analysis (select one: evaluate the Marmot Review's social gradient in health — apply the Whitehall studies (Marmot-Rose-Shipley 1978 and Marmot 1991): what is the psychosocial pathway hypothesis (relative status, control, social support) vs the material pathway for the civil service gradient? Evaluate the evidence on the relative contributions of material deprivation, psychosocial stress, and health behaviors to the social gradient; what interventions at which social determinant level have the strongest evidence base?; evaluate place-based health disparities — apply the Robert Wood Johnson Foundation County Health Rankings model: what structural determinants (income inequality, educational attainment, unemployment, housing quality, food access, built environment) explain county-level health outcome variation? Apply to a specific regional context (Appalachia, the Deep South, or an urban-rural comparison); what cross-sector policies (housing vouchers, SNAP, earned income tax credit) have the strongest evidence for improving health outcomes through social determinants pathways?; evaluate the ACA's prevention and public health provisions — apply the Prevention and Public Health Fund and community transformation grants: what is the evidence that investing in primary prevention (tobacco cessation, obesity prevention, vaccinations) reduces downstream acute care spending? Evaluate the Return on Investment for prevention vs treatment using the Maciosek et al. clinical preventive services rankings)",
